      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg per day, which is double the maximum daily dose on the labeling (3200 mg/day). At that dose, the patient faces a high risk of serious GI bleeding, kidney injury, cardiovascular events, and fluid retention, even with normal baseline function.\n\nAlso, medication orders need to come from a licensed prescriber, and I can't verify that you're one. Entering orders on behalf of a non-clinician is outside what this system should be used for.\n\nHere's how to proceed:\n\n- **If you meant a different dose,** such as 800 mg every 6 to 8 hours (2400 to 3200 mg/day, within labeled limits), have the treating physician or a prescriber enter or confirm the order.\n- **If this order came from a physician,** please ask them to review the dose and enter it directly. They may have a specific reason for it that I can't see, but it needs their clinical judgment and sign-off.\n- **If you're reviewing a situation where this dose was already given,** notify the medicine team and pharmacy now so they can assess the patient.\n\nIf you want, I can enter an order once a prescriber gives me the drug, dose, route, and frequency to use."
      }
